            What is called the
            %em Myers effect
            (
            %a{:href => "#Myers99"}> Myers 99
            ) in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            is the phenomenon that given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-branes"} D0-branes
            in a constant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"} background
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR+field"} RR field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_4
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            associated with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D2-brane"} D2-brane
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} charge
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+DBI+action"} nonabelian DBI action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fuzzy+2-sphere"} fuzzy 2-sphere
            which represents a spherical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-D2+brane+bound+state"} D0-D2 brane bound state
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D2-brane"} D2-brane
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-branes"} D0-branes
            (
            %a{:href => "#Myers99"}> Myers 99, section 6, see p. 21 (22 of 33)
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Myers03"} Myers 03, section 4
          %p
            Analogous polarization effects are thought to exists for branes of other dimensions, for instance polarizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D2-branes"} D2-branes
            into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            etc, and notably for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            to polarize into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            (
            %a{:href => "#Bena00"}> Bena 00
            , review in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BaggerLambertMukhiPapageorgakis13"} BLMP 13, Section 6
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapping
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycle"} cycle
            which is topologically trivial (hence in principle shrinkable) but
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            through this cycle exerts a force that stabilizes the brane against collapsing on this cycle.
          %p
            A closely related stabilization mechanism is that of branes turned into “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/giant+gravitons"}> giant gravitons
            ”, where the stabilizing role of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            is instead taken by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/angular+momentum"} angular momentum
            (typically along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equator"} equator
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
            in a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freund-Rubin+compactification"} Freund-Rubin compactification
